{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1337988-gods-n-monsters-how-would-you-build-a","id":1337988,"title":"Gods n Monsters - How Would You Build a...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-26T08:43:01-07:00","id":1337988,"title":"Gods n Monsters - How Would You Build a...","content":"Inspired by the Gods &amp; Monsters supplement for M20 I'm wondering how you would build a fantasy or mythological character. No need to do all the stats but I'm very interested in combining various Merits, flaws, and Special Advantages to get an interesting combination.<br /> <br /> e.g.<br /> <br /> Liche: Simply add &quot;Immortal&quot; (7pt merit) with Phylactery (7pt flaw) to a sphere-using Mage<br /> <br /> Mummy: A basic &quot;Immortal&quot; (7pt merit)<br /> <br /> <br /> Adding Rapid Healing (various) and Soak Lethal (3pt merit) makes any creature extremely resilient as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 09-26-2019, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T10:15:58-07:00","id":1338003,"title":"","content":"Blood Mage/Magic Vampire: give them the blood mage flaw and a 'free health pool of 10' to represent vampire blood (We are trying to avoid using VTM rules). Give them the same type of rules that sorcerers have, copy a few effects off the common magick chart, but with a few differences:<br /> 1: A majority of these don't require a ritual to do, they just take a turn. (Some of the more complicated ones might require more blood + a ritual)<br /> 2: They don't generate paradox like a sorcerer.<br /> 3: They cost blood.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of 'represent Vampire magic with spheres' as that makes it very broad and better than regular vampire magic, so I think 'give them shit off the common magick chart' is a good compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}